    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born in 1890 in upstate New York, Aisling Sturbridge taught herself Latin and Greek to pursue the occult before fleeing to London, where she caught the attention of Aleister Crowley and, more happily, the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} Lucien de Maupassant, who Embraced her in Vienna in 1911 after rescuing her from Crowley's designs. She served decades as a free agent between chantries, tended chantries through the London Blitz, and lost track of her missing sire in 1948. Field-promoted to lieutenant and then High Regent of the Chantry of the Five Boroughs after the Battle of New York, she has become one of the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere}'s most popular and effective regents &mdash; and, to conservative elders, one of its most worrying loose cannons, given her willingness to work openly with other clans and her total disinterest in claiming the princedom herself.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Assume nothing, verify everything, and never let a barrier go untested. You never stop quietly searching for word of your lost sire, Lucien de Maupassant.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Lucien de Maupassant (missing since 1948). Thaumaturgical Paths (Storyteller discretion): Path of Blood 5, Movement of the Mind 5, Lure of Flames 4, Elemental Mastery 3, Countermagic 2, Spirit Manipulation 2, Technomancy 3. Merits: Time Sense, Natural Linguist. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
